# a URL is never made only where one walk of its construction stands in front of every read. Where the construction is walked several times and a read stands behind them all, one name stands for what each walk has built:
# no text answers for it, so every walk makes the object as written
# f2: two turns written out. f3: a block that the ways of a closed arm walk apart from the others
# f1: every turn of a typed build of this loop would leave it, so the builds are undone and the loop is built once: the one walk that is kept stands in front of the read, and the URL is never made where its text is plain
# f4 and f5: the URL is still never made: in f4 each copy of the loop reads its own, in f5 the one construction stands in front of both copies
# each function is handed to code that nobody has seen
# f1 = leftByReturn, f2 = twoTurns, f3 = walkedApart, f4 = readInside, f5 = madeInFront
# -- source: url-read-behind-several-walks-of-its-construction-is-made.ts
